---
beermat: 1
title: Built-in units
---

# Built-in units

Every unit Beermat knows, defined in its own linear syntax and evaluated once at startup.
Each definition may use the units above it. The seven SI base units (`m`, `kg`, `s`, `A`,
`K`, `mol`, `cd`), the constant `π` and the built-in functions are defined in code.

A user definition with the same name shadows a unit in the sheet, but inside a unit
placeholder (`= ? m`) the name still means the unit. See [docs/units.md](../../../../../../../docs/units.md).

## Length

```calc
mm := 0.001 m
cm := 0.01 m
km := 1000 m
μm := 1e-6 m
in := 0.0254 m
ft := 12 in
yd := 3 ft
mi := 5280 ft
```

## Time and frequency

```calc
ms := 0.001 s
min := 60 s
sec := s
hr := 60 min
h := hr
mph := mi/hr
kph := km/hr
day := 24 hr
week := 7 day
yr := 365.2422 day
Hz := 1/s
kHz := 1000 Hz
MHz := 1e6 Hz
```

## Angle

Angles are dimensionless, unless a sheet makes them a dimension (`angle: dimension`), when `rad` is its unit.

```calc
rad := 1
deg := π/180
rev := 2*π
gon := π/200
```

## Ratios

`%` is a hundredth: `ξ := 5 %`. It is written in backticks in the text, since `%` can't start a plain name.

```calc
`%` := 0.01
```

## Mass

`g` is gravity (below); the gram is the upright `\rm g`, drawn upright like
every unit. `mg` is the milligram.

```calc
\rm g := 0.001 kg
mg := 0.000001 kg
t := 1000 kg
tonne := t
lb := 0.45359237 kg
ton := 2000 lb
```

## Temperature

`°C` and `°F` are points on a scale: `20 °C` is 293.15 K, and `= ? °C` shows a temperature
on the scale. Here they are one degree; each scale's zero is built in. A temperature difference is
`Δ°C` or `Δ°F`, and `R` is the rankine.

```calc
°C := K
°F := 5/9*K
Δ°C := K
Δ°F := 5/9*K
R := 5/9*K
```

## Acceleration

```calc
g := 9.80665 m/s^2
```

## Force

```calc
N := kg*m/s^2
kN := 1000 N
MN := 1e6 N
GN := 1e9 N
kgf := kg*g
tonnef := tonne*g
lbf := lb*g
kip := 1000 lbf
```

## Pressure and stress

```calc
Pa := N/m^2
kPa := 1000 Pa
MPa := 1e6 Pa
GPa := 1e9 Pa
bar := 1e5 Pa
atm := 101325 Pa
psi := lbf/in^2
ksi := 1000 psi
```

## Energy and power

```calc
J := N*m
joule := J
kJ := 1000 J
MJ := 1e6 J
GJ := 1e9 J
W := J/s
kW := 1000 W
MW := 1e6 W
GW := 1e9 W
BTU := 1055.05585262 J
hp := 550 ft*lbf/s
```

## Volume

```calc
L := 0.001 m^3
mL := 0.001 L
gal := 3.785411784 L
```

## Electrical

```calc
mA := 0.001 A
C := A*s
V := W/A
volt := V
kV := 1000 V
Ω := V/A
ohm := Ω
S := 1/Ω
F := C/V
Wb := V*s
T := Wb/m^2
H := Wb/A
mH := 0.001*H
```

## Light, radiation, chemistry

```calc
lm := cd
lx := lm/m^2
Bq := 1/s
Gy := J/kg
Sv := J/kg
kat := mol/s
```
